## S8. Step 6: Decision

**Status:** NEW | **Priority:** P0 | **PRD:** UW-1..4, UW-6

A processing state ("Assessing your application") leads to **one of four outcome views**. Outcome is driven by the mock PAN (see §3).

| Outcome | What the borrower sees | Next |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Approved** | Confirmation, final rate, amount, tenure | S9 |
| **Counter-offer** | Revised amount / tenure / rate with plain-language reason(s). Actions: Accept revised, Modify, Withdraw | S9, S6, or S2 |
| **Referred** | "Under review" with expected turnaround; application appears on S2 as Referred | S2 (officer decides in S13) |
| **Declined** | Principal reasons in plain language, downloadable summary, what could change the outcome where policy allows. No dead end | S2 |

**Engine (behind the screen):** bureau pull (mock, uses the consent captured in S7) → policy rules (score bands, FOIR, age gates, negative list, RC mismatch, LTV recheck) → decision + reason codes + rule version stored. **Rules:** deterministic and explainable. No "AI" wording. Reason codes are internal; the borrower sees plain-language text. **Data out:** `decision {outcome, reasonCodes[], finalRate, finalAmount, finalTenure, ruleVersion, bureauSummary}`.

