## S10. Step 8: Pre-disbursal & Disbursal

**Status:** NEW | **Priority:** P0 | **PRD:** PRE-1..3, DIS-1..3

### 10a. Pre-disbursal checklist

Each item shows Pending / Verified / Failed.

| Case | Checklist items |
| --- | --- |
| All | Comprehensive insurance with lender's hypothecation noted |
| New | Dealer invoice matches quotation · margin money (down payment) received by dealer |
| Used, from dealer | Inspection/valuation report · dealer invoice |
| Used, from individual | Seller KYC · transfer papers (Forms 29/30) · seller consent |
| Active hypothecation | Existing-loan closure proof · NOC · Form 35 |

**Inspection outcome (used):** a value drop (e.g. −8%) re-runs LTV and may reduce the loan amount. Show revised figures and require **re-acceptance** if the amount changes.

### 10b. Disbursal

Shows **beneficiary** (dealer/seller name, masked account) and amount. Never shown as paid to an intermediary or agent. Mock "Release funds" (demo action).

### 10c. Post-disbursal timeline and cooling-off

- Timeline: Disbursed → hypothecation initiated at RTO (Form 34) → RC with HP endorsement received (mock upload) → Complete.
- **Cooling-off window** (config, minimum 1 day, disclosed in KFS): "Exit without penalty" action showing principal + proportionate interest, and any disclosed one-time processing fee. Confirm step before exit; status becomes Cooled-off.

**Data out:** `checklist[]`, `disbursal {beneficiary, amount, date}`, `hypothecation {status}`.

